First of all, let's start with what we agree on.  We need childrens books for people to start with, and Alice in Wonderland hardly qualifies.

You say our objectives differ radically.  My point was that there need to be clearly defines target audiences and clearly defined objectives - whatever they are.  You sound as if you know what you want, and that's great!  I suspect that was obvious to you to begin with so forgive me for saying the obvious.  There is an awful lot of websites out there whose objectives are mushy at best.

Good marketing requires BOTH form and content - not either or.  I would never put form over content.  In fact I've spent a lifetime fighting "sizzle without the steak".  The reason I suggested we need to focus on form is that there is plenty of great content but, after 20 years, the number of people particpating in the content is "below critical mass" (highly subjective on my part!).  Needless to say, I'm speaking on my behalf only.  I'm sure my views are a miniscule minoity within the lojban community - but I hope that will change.

Good luck with you website anyway.

mu'u mi'e .andrus.

